WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.560
Want to see your app on a phone?

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.106
You do not need a phone.

3
00:00:04.106 --> 00:00:06.746
You do not need Android Studio, or Xcode.

4
00:00:06.746 --> 00:00:09.450
One command opens a phone in your browser.

5
00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.547
Open a terminal in your app folder.

6
00:00:13.547 --> 00:00:16.758
Type npx shipvo run android, and press Enter.

7
00:00:16.758 --> 00:00:19.398
Shipvo builds a web copy of your app.

8
00:00:19.398 --> 00:00:20.825
It needs no account.

9
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.603
Your browser opens on a page with a phone in the middle.

10
00:00:27.603 --> 00:00:32.298
A label says Simulated, because this is a copy of a phone, not a real one.

11
00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.075
Click it like you would tap.

12
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:39.628
Want an iPhone instead?

13
00:00:39.628 --> 00:00:40.245
Type ios.

14
00:00:40.245 --> 00:00:43.607
You get the iPhone look, with its Dynamic Island.

15
00:00:43.607 --> 00:00:46.420
The page scales the phone to your window.

16
00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:50.125
Add ?dark=1 to the address for the dark frame.

17
00:00:51.725 --> 00:00:52.945
Now the best part.

18
00:00:52.945 --> 00:00:57.013
Your AI assistant can drive the same phone while you watch.

19
00:00:57.013 --> 00:01:03.182
While shipvo run is up, the assistant calls open_app, and finds your live phone.

20
00:01:03.182 --> 00:01:05.012
It taps, types and scrolls.

21
00:01:05.012 --> 00:01:06.300
You see every move.

22
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.141
Need another port?

23
00:01:09.141 --> 00:01:10.451
Add --port.

24
00:01:10.451 --> 00:01:12.312
Want a real emulator later?

25
00:01:12.312 --> 00:01:13.759
Add --native.

26
00:01:13.759 --> 00:01:17.275
When you are done, press Ctrl+C in the terminal.

27
00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:20.699
That is it.

28
00:01:20.699 --> 00:01:23.314
A phone in your browser, in seconds.

29
00:01:23.314 --> 00:01:26.654
Try npx shipvo run android in your app folder.

30
00:01:26.654 --> 00:01:29.850
The guide is at shipvo.dev/learn.
